## Failed image downloads (noted in-page per instructions)

8 images failed to download — all from the same root cause: URLs under `/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/...` on www.dietz.eu now 301-redirect to the site homepage (dead/removed assets), and the `relaunch.dietz.eu` fallback subdomain that hosts some older media no longer resolves in DNS (confirmed NXDOMAIN via DNS-over-HTTPS lookup) — so there is no working fallback host. These are genuinely broken image links on the live production site, not a local/network issue. Noted inline in the affected pages:

- reference/pages/en/products/hybrid-assemblies.md — 5 failed images (Baugruppen-Montage-0001-WEB.jpg, -0002, -0003, -0006, -0007)
- reference/pages/en/products/special-packaging.md — 3 failed images (Sonderverpackungen-0001-WEB.jpg, -0002, -0004)

## Other notes

- The dietz.eu site intermittently returned HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) during this run, most likely due to combined load from multiple concurrent chunk-processing sessions crawling the same site. All 429s were resolved by waiting ~20-60s and retrying; no URL was skipped because of this.
- Several category/product pages' internal links resolved to a `relaunch.dietz.eu` or German-slug staging host rather than the live `/en/` path — these are noted in the affected markdown files with the presumed live equivalent.
- The `/en/precision-springs/` glossary stub and `/en/products/precision-springs/` category page are two distinct pages on the site and were captured separately, as were the two "prototype-construction" style pages.
